{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA + scope expansion recorded (implementation in progress)\n\n**Root cause (proven, static/config defect).** `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors`\n(`infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf:35`) assigned neither `alarm_actions` nor `ok_actions`, so\nCloudWatch had no notification target and the OK -> ALARM transition delivered nothing. Confirmed\nstatically (grep returns nothing in the resource body) and live (`describe-alarms` -> `AlarmActions: []`).\n\n**Why this is a defect and not intended behaviour** — two in-repo authoritative citations:\n1. `monitoring.tf:205-207` describes an alarm 'created out-of-band with an EMPTY alarm_actions\n   list (so it never notified)' and says wiring SNS is 'closing the silent-alarm gap'. Empty\n   actions is named, in this repo's own IaC, as a gap to be closed.\n2. `monitoring_s4b.tf:19-21` — the alarm's own header claims it 'surfaces a persistently broken\n   voter to an operator'. The resource did not do what its own contract said.\n\nCounter-evidence considered and rejected: `monitoring_1fa8.tf:38-42` read 'mirrors S4b's\nvoter_errors alarm; UNLIKE S4b it WIRES SNS ... because a broken CI dispatcher silently blocks ALL\nsubmits'. That rationale is equally true of S4b under ADR-0013, so 1fa8's author observed the\nomission and rationalised it rather than fixing it — the convention was documented FROM the one\ninstance that did not follow it. That comment has been corrected in this change.\n\n**SCOPE EXPANDED — the sibling is included.** `replication_errors`\n(`infra/terraform/monitoring_s5.tf:30`) has the identical defect and had no ticket of its own.\nAn audit of all 13 `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` blocks shows 11 wire both actions to the shared\n`aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`; these two were the ONLY omissions. Both are fixed here rather than\nsplit, so there is one apply rather than two and the sibling is not rediscovered later. The\ndescription and `file_impact` were updated to cover both BEFORE the plan-review attestation was\nearned, so the reviewer saw the expanded scope.\n\n**No operator decision was required.** The destination is the established repo convention\n(`aws_sns_topic.alerts`), which already carries the operator's email subscription — not a new\ntarget to choose. The earlier 'needs a notification target' framing is superseded.\n\n**Guard added.** `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py` parses every alarm block under\n`infra/terraform/` and fails on any lacking `alarm_actions` (and separately `ok_actions`), with a\nmandatory anti-vacuity assertion and an explicit documented opt-out marker. Detail in the closing report.\n\n**APPLY STATUS: NOT YET APPLIED.** This comment records HCL work only. Landing terraform is not\napplying it (see [rebar:1c39-96d4-8f9e-4d38]) — the alarms still notify nobody until an operator runs apply."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785920546218991001,"uuid":"ad1915c6-91c5-4c28-a365-af359ee78b18"}